From 6e3434128336d67b5b610377a616bf4518120879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:27:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): show and edit the Hone feedback on Pi replies

A session holds one feedback in Hone. The pressed thumb under a Pi reply
shows its rating, and the comment under the newest reply expands to its
full text. Either thumb opens a popover with the comment filled in, so
Save replaces the feedback and the thumb pressed sets its rating. Remove
feedback clears it.

hone.feedback now takes the whole feedback, or null to clear it, and
calls Hone's POST or DELETE /api/traces/{id}/feedback.
hone.threadFeedback returns the feedback as a rating and a comment, so
only the server reads Hone's stored text.
